What an action changed, in the action's own result, and the tools the model
otherwise rebuilt in browser_console.

Symptoms (one long booking session, 308 browser calls): 128 browser_console
calls (617 s, 150 k chars), most of them `new Promise(setTimeout(...))` then
`document.body.innerText.slice(...)` after a click (50 model-chosen sleeps,
102 s), or a `querySelectorAll(...).find(innerText === ...).click()` for a
control with no ref; 41 of 63 clicks were followed by such a script and 16
by a screenshot, because a click answered only {clicked, url}; a six-digit
code went in as six browser_press calls; errors read "409 Client Error:
Conflict for url: http://127.0.0.1:<port>/tabs/<id>/evaluate (error:
Internal server error ...)".

- browser_click, x/y clicks and named-key browser_press return `changes`:
  the snapshot lines that changed since the model last saw the page
  (changes_kind diff) or the new page (changes_kind page, the URL changed or
  the diff is longer than half the page), at most 3000 chars, redacted and
  vault-masked like every snapshot. browser_navigate and browser_snapshot
  keep the baseline. A single-character press stays a bare press.
- browser_click text= (exact, nth): the visible element showing that text,
  in the page or a frame (camofox-browser's agent-actions.patch); several
  matches are refused with the list, nth picks one.
- browser_snapshot wait_for= (timeout, max 60 s): waits server-side for the
  text to show, then snapshots; the result says found and waited_s.
- browser_type without ref types key by key into the focused element.
- HTTP errors read as the server's own explanation (`HTTP 409: <error>;
  code; recovery`), without requests' "for url: <tab URL>" prefix.
Not upstream (hermes-official-plugins).

